# Auth, stores & routing

## Middleware

- Authenticated app pages: `definePageMeta({ middleware: ["local-pages"] })`
- Login page: `middleware: ["local-auth-user"]`
- Logic: [`local-pages.js`](mdc:app/middleware/local-pages.js) — login redirect + `canAccessPath`

## Role access (UI-only)

Allowlists in [`routeAccess.js`](mdc:app/utils/routeAccess.js). **API remains source of truth.**

| Role | Home |
|------|------|
| `ADMIN` | `/home` (all paths) |
| `BRANCH_EMPLOYEE` | `/sales/direct` |
| `CUSTOMER_SERVICE` | `/books/reserve` |

When adding a page for a non-admin role, update `canAccessPath` allowlists.

## Pinia

- Stores: [`app/store/auth.js`](mdc:app/store/auth.js), [`academicYear.js`](mdc:app/store/academicYear.js)
- Ids: `"authStore"`, `"academicYearStore"`; exports `useAuthStore` / `useAcademicYearStore`
- Options-style `defineStore` (`state` / `getters` / `actions`); token + academic year in localStorage
- Prefer [`useAuth`](mdc:app/composables/useAuth.js) / [`useAcademicYear`](mdc:app/composables/useAcademicYear.js) in UI

## Layouts

Role → layout via `USER_ROLE_LAYOUT` in [`userRole.js`](mdc:app/enums/userRole.js): `admin` | `branch-employee` | `customer-service` | `login`.
